The dual license above covers the program source — the Go code, wherever it
lives in the tree.

Everything else is marked `CC0-1.0` (public domain) so it can be copied and
adapted without obligation: the reusable workflows in .github/workflows/, the
GitLab CI/CD Catalog components in templates/, the shell scripts, the
Containerfiles, and all configuration, documentation, examples and test data.
These are the parts adopters are expected to lift into their own repositories,
and CC0 is what lets them do that freely.

Third-party files keep the license their authors gave them; the vendored
Gradle wrapper is Apache-2.0, for example.

This project follows the REUSE specification (https://reuse.software): every
file carries an SPDX license identifier, either in its header or in REUSE.toml.
That identifier, not this summary, is authoritative for any given file.
